      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Poseidon (2006) reimagines the disaster film classic <a href=\"/movie/551\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"551\">The Poseidon Adventure</a> (1972) with modern special effects and a more action-oriented approach. Director Wolfgang Petersen, who previously mastered maritime tension in <a href=\"/movie/387\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"387\">Das Boot</a> (1981) and <a href=\"/movie/2133\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"2133\">The Perfect Storm</a> (2000), brings his signature intensity to this claustrophobic survival thriller. The film follows a familiar disaster movie template established by films like <a href=\"/movie/5919\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"5919\">The Towering Inferno</a> (1974) and modernized by <a href=\"/movie/597\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"597\">Titanic</a> (1997) - gather a diverse group of characters, establish their relationships, then thrust them into catastrophe."
      },
